From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: G31_RenderOnlyFix <render-only@gpu31>
Date: Thu, 20 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gpu31-kms: Mode B render-ONLY minor on 3.10 DRM core (no
 card0)

Mode B gives a DRM render node (renderD128) for unprivileged GPU clients
(Mali/kbase shim now, panfrost later) while the DECON fbdev keeps the
panel.  v1 of this patch ADDED renderD128 next to the primary minor; the
int4 image proved that shape unshippable: drm_get_platform_dev allocated
BOTH card0 and renderD128 for panfrost7580, and Xorg auto-probes card0
and deadlocks in D state (blank screen, cursor dot).  This v2 makes the
panfrost7580 device register as render-only: NO card minor at all
(no /dev/dri/card0, no controlD node), only renderD128.  X's platform
probe scans card nodes only, so it can never see this device; Xorg stays
on fbdev exactly as on M1.

Allocation point (vendor 3.10 stub, drivers/gpu/drm/drm_platform.c,
drm_get_platform_dev): the legacy path unconditionally allocates the
primary minor via drm_get_minor(dev, &dev->primary, DRM_MINOR_LEGACY)
(pristine drm_platform.c:72), with controlD64 iff DRIVER_MODESET.  The
render carve-out (drm_stub.c drm_minor_get_id: base 128, limit
base+255, i.e. minors 128..383) was never allocated on the platform
path; v1 added it unconditionally after primary.  v2 branches on the new
DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY bit (0x8000, free on 3.10): when set, allocate ONLY
dev->render via DRM_MINOR_RENDER BEFORE ->load() (unwind on err_g3), and
skip primary/control, the legacy mode_group setup, and the primary-based
DRM_INFO.  Render-only consumes no primary idr slot; the exynos/G2D card0
(if present) keeps its legacy slot untouched.

Diff vs v1 (code/gpu31/kms/0001-*.patch): v1 allocated render IN ADDITION
to primary (both nodes on one device).  v2 allocates render INSTEAD OF
primary for DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY devices only; all other devices keep the
byte-identical legacy path.  Kept from v1 unchanged in intent: the
dev->render holder (include/drm/drmP.h), drm_stub.c put/unplug release,
drm_fops.c render-always-authenticated, drm_drv.c render-MASTER deny.
Hardened for the missing primary: stub teardown branches (no
drm_put_minor(NULL), no dev->primary deref), platform unwind legs
release exactly the minors allocated, DRM_INFO prints the render index
on the render-only path.

Hunks (context verified byte-exact against pristine-tree `cat -A`):

1. include/drm/drmP.h: add DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY 0x8000 + `struct drm_minor
*render` holder + comment.  3.10's struct drm_device has only
`primary`/`control`, so the minor pointer must live somewhere; the
device struct keeps the platform/stub unwind paths symmetric with
primary/control (no exynos driver patch needed).

2. drivers/gpu/drm/drm_platform.c (drm_get_platform_dev):
DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY -> drm_get_minor(dev, &dev->render, DRM_MINOR_RENDER)
only, BEFORE ->load(); legacy path untouched otherwise.  New unwind:
err_g3 releases render / primary respectively, err_g2 releases control
only on the non-render-only MODESET path.

3. drivers/gpu/drm/drm_stub.c (drm_put_dev / drm_unplug_dev):
release/unplug ->render (NULL-guarded; dev is kzalloc'd so the field
starts NULL and drm_get_minor NULLs it on failure) on render-only
devices; legacy put/unplug of primary/control otherwise untouched
(including the MODESET-gated control release, now also gated on
!RENDER_ONLY).

4. drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fops.c (drm_open_helper): render opens are
always authenticated, mirroring upstream render-node semantics of that
era (render client is authenticated, just never master).  Card0
behaviour is unchanged: non-root clients still authenticate via the
AUTH_MAGIC dance.

5. drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c (drm_ioctl dispatcher): explicit deny of any
DRM_MASTER-flagged ioctl arriving on a render node, even from the
render-minor master.  This clause is REQUIRED: mastership is per-minor
(drm_open_helper creates minor->master on first open of EACH node), so
the first render opener becomes master of the render minor and would
pass the plain `DRM_MASTER && !is_master` test.  With this clause,
SETCRTC/SETPLANE/CURSOR/ATTACH/DETACH/SETPROPERTY/PAGE_FLIP/DIRTYFB/
OBJ_SETPROPERTY (all DRM_MASTER) return -EACCES on renderD128: render
cannot modeset, without any new flag.  The existing
`!CONTROL_ALLOW && type == CONTROL -> -EACCES` control-node gate is
untouched, and buffer/GEM/PRIME/read-only-KMS ioctls keep working from
the render node under their existing DRM_AUTH/DRM_ROOT_ONLY bits.

Driver companion (code/gpu31/driver/0001-*.patch): panfrost7580 sets
`.driver_features = DRIVER_GEM | DRIVER_PRIME | DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY`
(no DRIVER_MODESET as before).  No other driver change is needed: the
core branches on the bit; the driver never touches dev->primary.

fbdev non-conflict statement:
- No DT change: this patch matches no `samsung,exynos7580-decon-drm`,
  `samsung,exynos7580-dsim`, `samsung,exynos5-decon_driver`,
  `samsung,exynos5-dsim`, or `samsung,exynos5-mipi-dsi` compatible, binds
  no DECON/DSIM registers, takes no clocks/regulators/power domains, and
  installs no IRQ.  The vendor `decon_driver` (late_initcall) keeps its
  nodes; /dev/fb0 + fbdev X are unaffected.
- Not Mode A (M1-safe path already built): M1's card0+controlD64 via
  exynos+G2D stands alone.  This patch only ADDS renderD128 next to it.
- Not Mode C (full KMS later): Mode C still requires the separate
  exynos7580 DECON/DSIM + panel patches (code/gpu31/series/0001-...-kms)
  PLUS the DT compatible flip PLUS the vendor-fbdev Kconfig off-switches,
  applied together.  None of that is in this patch.

X-probe rationale (why card0 must not exist): Xorg's platform probe
enumerates /dev/dri/cardN only (never renderD128); with a panfrost card0
present it binds the modesetting driver, issues modeset ioctls against a
node with no CRTC/encoder/connector, and wedges in D state.  With no card
node for panfrost7580 at all, the probe finds only the exynos/G2D card0
(M1 shape) or nothing, and Xorg falls back to the fbdev driver pinned by
j7elte-gpu-soft/10-fbdev.conf -- the proven M1 UI path.

Boot-path render-node audit: nothing in the boot path opens the render
node.  Xorg is pinned to fbdev (`Driver "fbdev"`, `/dev/fb0`) and never
touches /dev/dri/renderD128; no udev rule, init script, or userspace
component in-tree references renderD128 (only probe/selftest tools open
it explicitly, off-boot).  The node idles unopened until the first GPU
client (Mesa/kbase-shim/selftest) opens it.

Verification (host-side only; no build/flash in shared tree per slice rules):
- `git apply --check` clean on pristine-tree copies of the 5 files
  (integrator re-runs at build time).
- Per-file `gcc -fsyntax-only` AND real `-c` object compile with the
  recorded kbuild flags vs actual 3.10.108 headers: all 4 patched `.c`
  files pass with zero warnings (drmP.h is covered through inclusion).
- apply-check + compile evidence recorded in
  docs/reports/gpu31-render-only.md.
- On-device (post-int5-build, M1Verify-owned): `ls /dev/dri` shows
  renderD128 and NO card0 from panfrost; fbdev X stays 720x1280;
  unprivileged PRIME HANDLE_TO_FD + GEM map works from the render fd;
  SETCRTC from the render fd returns -EACCES.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c      |  5 +++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fops.c     |  9 +++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_platform.c | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_stub.c     | 18 ++++++++++++---
 include/drm/drmP.h             | 11 +++++++++++
 5 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c
@@ -436,6 +436,11 @@
 	} else if (((ioctl->flags & DRM_ROOT_ONLY) && !capable(CAP_SYS_ADMIN)) ||
 		   ((ioctl->flags & DRM_AUTH) && !file_priv->authenticated) ||
 		   ((ioctl->flags & DRM_MASTER) && !file_priv->is_master) ||
+		   /* Render-only: a render node can never be modeset master,
+		    * not even the first opener (per-minor master would
+		    * otherwise pass the DRM_MASTER test above). */
+		   ((file_priv->minor->type == DRM_MINOR_RENDER) &&
+		    (ioctl->flags & DRM_MASTER)) ||
 		   (!(ioctl->flags & DRM_CONTROL_ALLOW) && (file_priv->minor->type == DRM_MINOR_CONTROL))) {
 		retcode = -EACCES;
 	} else {
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fops.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fops.c
@@ -274,6 +274,15 @@
 	priv->ioctl_count = 0;
 	/* for compatibility root is always authenticated */
 	priv->authenticated = capable(CAP_SYS_ADMIN);
+	/*
+	 * Render-only: a render node has no privileged modeset state behind
+	 * it, so the opener is authenticated from the start (upstream render
+	 * semantics of the era: authenticated, just never master). Card0
+	 * behaviour is unchanged: non-root clients still authenticate via
+	 * the AUTH_MAGIC dance.
+	 */
+	if (priv->minor && priv->minor->type == DRM_MINOR_RENDER)
+		priv->authenticated = 1;
 	priv->lock_count = 0;
 
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&priv->lhead);
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_platform.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_platform.c
@@ -63,15 +63,30 @@
 		goto err_g1;
 	}
 
-	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET)) {
-		ret = drm_get_minor(dev, &dev->control, DRM_MINOR_CONTROL);
+	/* Mode B render-only (panfrost7580, DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY): allocate
+	 * ONLY the render minor (DRM_MINOR_RENDER, idr carve-out base 128
+	 * -> /dev/dri/renderD128 via the already-wired drm_sysfs.c
+	 * renderD%d naming). No primary (/dev/dri/cardN) and no control
+	 * node, so the X platform probe (which scans cardN only) can never
+	 * see this device -- Xorg stays on fbdev. BEFORE ->load() so a
+	 * failed bring-up unwinds the node too. Non-render-only devices
+	 * keep the exact legacy path (control iff MODESET, then primary). */
+	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY)) {
+		ret = drm_get_minor(dev, &dev->render, DRM_MINOR_RENDER);
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_g1;
-	}
+	} else {
+		if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET)) {
+			ret = drm_get_minor(dev, &dev->control,
+					    DRM_MINOR_CONTROL);
+			if (ret)
+				goto err_g1;
+		}
 
-	ret = drm_get_minor(dev, &dev->primary, DRM_MINOR_LEGACY);
-	if (ret)
-		goto err_g2;
+		ret = drm_get_minor(dev, &dev->primary, DRM_MINOR_LEGACY);
+		if (ret)
+			goto err_g2;
+	}
 
 	if (dev->driver->load) {
 		ret = dev->driver->load(dev, 0);
@@ -80,7 +95,8 @@
 	}
 
 	/* setup the grouping for the legacy output */
-	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET)) {
+	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET) &&
+	    !drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY)) {
 		ret = drm_mode_group_init_legacy_group(dev,
 				&dev->primary->mode_group);
 		if (ret)
@@ -91,16 +107,27 @@
 
 	mutex_unlock(&drm_global_mutex);
 
-	DRM_INFO("Initialized %s %d.%d.%d %s on minor %d\n",
-		 driver->name, driver->major, driver->minor, driver->patchlevel,
-		 driver->date, dev->primary->index);
+	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY))
+		DRM_INFO("Initialized %s %d.%d.%d %s on minor %d (render-only)\n",
+			 driver->name, driver->major, driver->minor,
+			 driver->patchlevel, driver->date,
+			 dev->render->index);
+	else
+		DRM_INFO("Initialized %s %d.%d.%d %s on minor %d\n",
+			 driver->name, driver->major, driver->minor,
+			 driver->patchlevel, driver->date,
+			 dev->primary->index);
 
 	return 0;
 
 err_g3:
-	drm_put_minor(&dev->primary);
+	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY))
+		drm_put_minor(&dev->render);
+	else
+		drm_put_minor(&dev->primary);
 err_g2:
-	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET))
+	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET) &&
+	    !drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY))
 		drm_put_minor(&dev->control);
 err_g1:
 	kfree(dev);
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_stub.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_stub.c
@@ -476,13 +476,23 @@
 
 	drm_ctxbitmap_cleanup(dev);
 
-	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET))
+	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET) &&
+	    !drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY))
 		drm_put_minor(&dev->control);
 
 	if (driver->driver_features & DRIVER_GEM)
 		drm_gem_destroy(dev);
 
-	drm_put_minor(&dev->primary);
+	/* Render-only devices never allocated a primary/control minor:
+	 * release the render node instead. Non-render-only devices keep
+	 * the legacy path. (dev is kzalloc'd so dev->render starts NULL;
+	 * the NULL guard covers the hypothetical pre-alloc failure.) */
+	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY)) {
+		if (dev->render)
+			drm_put_minor(&dev->render);
+	} else {
+		drm_put_minor(&dev->primary);
+	}
 
 	list_del(&dev->driver_item);
 	kfree(dev->devname);
@@ -493,9 +503,15 @@
 void drm_unplug_dev(struct drm_device *dev)
 {
 	/* for a USB device */
-	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET))
+	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET) &&
+	    !drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY))
 		drm_unplug_minor(dev->control);
-	drm_unplug_minor(dev->primary);
+	if (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY)) {
+		if (dev->render)
+			drm_unplug_minor(dev->render);
+	} else {
+		drm_unplug_minor(dev->primary);
+	}
 
 	mutex_lock(&drm_global_mutex);
 
--- a/include/drm/drmP.h
+++ b/include/drm/drmP.h
@@ -156,6 +156,11 @@
 #define DRIVER_GEM         0x1000
 #define DRIVER_MODESET     0x2000
 #define DRIVER_PRIME       0x4000
+/* Render-only device: no primary or control minor, only the render node.
+ * Checked by drm_get_platform_dev (this patch) and the panfrost7580
+ * platform driver (sets the bit). 0x8000 is free on 3.10 (no other
+ * DRIVER_* bit uses it; verified against pristine drmP.h). */
+#define DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY 0x8000
 
 #define DRIVER_BUS_PCI 0x1
 #define DRIVER_BUS_PLATFORM 0x2
@@ -1207,6 +1212,12 @@
 	unsigned int agp_buffer_token;
 	struct drm_minor *control;		/**< Control node for card */
 	struct drm_minor *primary;		/**< render type primary screen head */
+	struct drm_minor *render;		/**< Render node (Mode B render-only):
+						 * GEM/PRIME/unprivileged GPU clients;
+						 * no modeset, never owns the display
+						 * pipe. Allocated by
+						 * drm_get_platform_dev when
+						 * DRIVER_RENDER_ONLY is set. */
 
         struct drm_mode_config mode_config;	/**< Current mode config */
 
